<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Armagnac</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Counts of Armagnac</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Armagnac was a noble family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>, counts of Armagnac from the 10th century and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rodez">Rodez</a> from 1302. Count Bernard VII led the Armagnac party in the French civil war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundians">Burgundians</a> until his murder in 1418. A cadet branch, the dukes of Nemours, also held La <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xi">Louis XI</a> had Jacques d'Armagnac executed in 1477, and the main line ended in 1497.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-armagnac.jpg" alt="House of Armagnac" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_comte_fr_Armagnac.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
